      "icon": "mobile"
    },
    {
      "id": "acfit2g4",
      "title": "Key decisions",
      "rows": [
        {
          "id": "y8pptexe",
          "layout": "1",
          "cells": [
            [
              {
                "id": "6i6grnfd",
                "kind": "heading",
                "level": 2,
                "text": "Four choices that shaped it"
              },
              {
                "id": "529luxx3",
                "kind": "paragraph",
                "text": "Write the thinking here — what you decided and why."
              },
              {
                "id": "bmr9y8qb",
                "kind": "list",
                "items": [
                  "Trimming lives inside the edit screen, not a separate step. The brief asked for fewer clicks, so the trimmer is where the preview already is.",
                  "The five minute limit is a rule on the screen, not a wall in the flow. It is shown where trimming happens, so it guides rather than interrupts.",
                  "Multi-select from the first screen. Posting is usually more than one clip, so the flow is built for a batch, not repeated for each video.",
                  "Processing was moved to the background. Instead of holding the user on an upload screen, pressing Post returns them to the feed immediately and a toast confirms when the videos are live. Their time back is worth more than a progress bar."
                ]
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "icon": "target"
    },
    {
      "id": "1shedfvw",
      "title": "Outcome",
      "rows": [
        {
          "id": "t5t8zh1g",
          "layout": "1",
          "cells": [
            [
              {
                "id": "wlhp1inm",
                "kind": "heading",
                "level": 2,
                "text": "The result"
              },
              {
                "id": "scry57bh",
                "kind": "paragraph",
                "text": "Pleny hired me after this task, and I went on to work on the app itself. The strongest thing a design task can prove is not a screen. It is that the thinking behind the screen was worth betting a role on."
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "icon": "flag"
